    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0727" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg715"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant General Alvan C. Gillem, Jr., to Brigadier
                        General Henry A. Byroade, at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-30">30 March 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>403. At Committee of Three meeting General Chang<anchor n="46" xml:id="d344-f1"/>
                    assured me that instructions regarding the field teams would be passed to
                    Northeast Headquarters. 1289 refers. Again yesterday morning Colonel Pee<anchor
                        n="47" xml:id="d344-f2"/> assured me that instructions had been issued. Last
                    night I saw the Gimo who said he would personally take up the matter.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d344-f1" n="46" xml:id="d344-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Chang Chih-chung, Chinese Government member of the Committee of Three.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d344-f2" n="47" xml:id="d344-f2-content">
                <p>Col. Peter T. K. Pee, aide to Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
